    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    Warren writes regarding his anthology <title>The Good Life</title> and asks to include Frank Prewett's poem <title>Be Kind to Animals</title> from <title>Poems</title>. 
                    He enquires what the fee would be for publishing in Britain and the World and the USA.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName key="Q676067">
                        <settlement>Braintree</settlement>
                        <region>Essex</region>
                        </placeName>
                        <date when="1944-09-12">12 September 1944</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine><orgName key="Q1623362">The Hogarth Press</orgName>,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Pixmore Avenue.</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Letchworth, Herts'.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>Dear Sirs,</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    I am editing an Anthology called <title>THE GOOD LIFE</title>
                    <note><p>This book came out in 1946, published by Eyre and Spottiswoode. 
                            The full title was The Good Life: 
                            An Anthology of the Life and Work of the Countryside, 
                            in Prose and Poetry.</p></note>,<lb/>
                    to be published next year by <orgName key="Q5422976">Messrs Eyre and Spottiswoode</orgName>,<lb/>
                    and wish to include the following poem:<lb/>
                    
                    <persName key="Q1257757">Frank Prewett</persName>: <title>Be Kind to Animals</title> (from <title>Poems</title>
                    <note><p>Poems refers to the collection of poems by Frank Prewett, published in 1921, 
                            which is the only book written by a Canadian to be published by the Hogarth Press.</p></note>)<lb/>
                    
                   If permission can be granted, would you kindly let me know<lb/>
                   the fee required covering (a) Britain and the World, and<lb/>
                   (b) the U.S.A. I am not sure yet whether we shall be able<lb/>
                   to publish in the U.S.A., but we shall make every effort<lb/>
                   to place the volume there.
                </p>
                <p>
                       We shall, of course, make the fullest acknowlegde-<lb/>
                       ment to Author and Publisher.
                </p>
                <p><add place="below" type="handwriting">
                        <unclear reason="bad handwriting">"I been in touch</unclear> with<lb/>
                        author for <unclear reason="bad handwriting">some time</unclear><lb/>
                        <unclear reason="bad handwriting">but that</unclear> we can <unclear reason="bad handwriting">handle</unclear><lb/>
                        his rights<lb/>
                        Suggest 1.1.0 for B.E. <unclear reason="bad handwriting">nature or</unclear><lb/>
                        1.1.0 for U.S.A."
                        <note><p>The unclear handwritten annotation was added by The Hogarth Press.</p></note>
                </add>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Yours faithfully,</salute>
                    <signed>C. Henry Warren</signed>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>Timbers,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Finchingfield,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Nr. Braintree,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Essex.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
